    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d535">

                <pb facs="1037" n="1025" xml:id="pg1025"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to Mr. Walter S. Robertson, at
                        Peiping</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-12">12 June 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>877. Yeh<anchor n="59" xml:id="d535-f1"/> informs Chou that Nationalist in
                    Operations [Division] stated Tu Li-ming will resume advance, attack, pursuit on
                    10th and then withdrew from meeting. Is this a fact? Rush reply.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d535-f1" n="59" xml:id="d535-f1-content">
                <p>Gen. Yeh Chien-ying, Chinese Communist Commissioner of the Executive Headquarters
                    at Peiping.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
